Source: fontz.inc
     1 				; Typefaces (part of image Z). Character > Font loads an Atari 8x8 charset file (.FNT, 1024 bytes in OS screen-code order,
     2 				; as written by the font editor) into bank 3 and sets it for the paragraph at the cursor. A change table (fpi/fps) maps
     3 				; paragraph numbers to font slots, so a font is a per-paragraph property and can never change inside a line. The table is
     4 				; saved in the CPG1 trailer: tag 2 = font of paragraph 0, tag 3 = [paragraph u16][name] for later changes (docs/PAGE.md).
     5 				; Slot 0 is the OS ROM set; the zoom view (zoom.inc) draws each line with its paragraph's slot.
     6
     7 				; Character > Font: ask for a file name (fop 9, handled by dofile -> fnload)
     8 5DF7 A9 09		hface lda #9
     9 5DF9 8D 11 14		 sta fop
    10 5DFC 4C C1 2B		 jmp fask
    11
